{"name":"Caudalie","deep":true,"image":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/0/05/Boutique_caudalie_camden.jpg","credit":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Boutique_caudalie_camden.jpg","caption":"Caudalie","source":"Wikimedia Commons via Wikipedia"},"mentions":0,"casual":{"lead":["Caudalie is a French skincare brand founded in 1995 by Mathilde and Bertrand Thomas in Bordeaux. Its products are built around polyphenols from grape seeds and vines, marketed for antioxidant, hydrating, brightening and anti-ageing care.","People use its serums, mists and creams as part of a skincare routine aimed at smoother, more even, glowing skin."],"sections":[{"h":"How people use it","paras":["The range covers cleansers, serums, moisturisers, masks, body care and a facial mist, used as ordinary daily skincare. Lines include resveratrol-based anti-ageing products and Vinopure for oily skin."],"subs":[]},{"h":"Risks & side effects","paras":["As with any cosmetic, fragrance or botanical ingredients can irritate sensitive skin. Wikipedia notes its own article on the company has a promotional tone, so company-sourced claims warrant care."],"subs":[]}]},"gallery":[{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/0/05/Boutique_caudalie_camden.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","full":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/0/05/Boutique_caudalie_camden.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","title":"Boutique caudalie camden","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","creator":"Aurdigital","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Boutique_caudalie_camden.jpg","source":"Wikimedia Commons"},{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Caudalie%2C_Monmouth_Street%2C_Covent_Garden_02.jpg/960px-Caudalie%2C_Monmouth_Street%2C_Covent_Garden_02.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","full":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/5a/Caudalie%2C_Monmouth_Street%2C_Covent_Garden_02.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","title":"Caudalie, Monmouth Street, Covent Garden 02","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","creator":"Edward Hands","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Caudalie,_Monmouth_Street,_Covent_Garden_02.jpg","source":"Wikimedia Commons"},{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/LOGO_CAUDALIE_PRUNE.png/960px-LOGO_CAUDALIE_PRUNE.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","full":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/79/LOGO_CAUDALIE_PRUNE.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","title":"LOGO CAUDALIE PRUNE","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","creator":"Aurdigital","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:LOGO_CAUDALIE_PRUNE.png","source":"Wikimedia Commons"},{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/0/0a/Caudalie_Logo.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","full":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/0/0a/Caudalie_Logo.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","title":"Caudalie Logo","license":"Public domain","creator":"Mathilde Thomas","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Caudalie_Logo.jpg","source":"Wikimedia Commons"},{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Caudalie%2C_Monmouth_Street%2C_Covent_Garden_01.jpg/960px-Caudalie%2C_Monmouth_Street%2C_Covent_Garden_01.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","full":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/cb/Caudalie%2C_Monmouth_Street%2C_Covent_Garden_01.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","title":"Caudalie, Monmouth Street, Covent Garden 01","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","creator":"Edward Hands","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Caudalie,_Monmouth_Street,_Covent_Garden_01.jpg","source":"Wikimedia Commons"},{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0c/Caudalie_boutique_Saint-Sulpice.png/960px-Caudalie_boutique_Saint-Sulpice.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","full":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/0/0c/Caudalie_boutique_Saint-Sulpice.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","title":"Caudalie boutique Saint-Sulpice","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","creator":"Lisa Karaoui","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Caudalie_boutique_Saint-Sulpice.png","source":"Wikimedia Commons"},{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/Nouveau_Logo_Caudalie_2021.png/960px-Nouveau_Logo_Caudalie_2021.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","full":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/53/Nouveau_Logo_Caudalie_2021.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","title":"Nouveau Logo Caudalie 2021","license":"CC0","creator":"Caudalie","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nouveau_Logo_Caudalie_2021.png","source":"Wikimedia Commons"},{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/44/Caudalie_boutique_%C3%A0_Bruxelles.jpg/960px-Caudalie_boutique_%C3%A0_Bruxelles.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","full":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/44/Caudalie_boutique_%C3%A0_Bruxelles.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","title":"Caudalie boutique à Bruxelles","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","creator":"Lisa Karaoui","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Caudalie_boutique_%C3%A0_Bruxelles.jpg","source":"Wikimedia Commons"}],"links":{"studies":[],"trials":[],"label":null,"reddit":[],"forums":[],"news":[],"social":[],"web":[{"title":"Caudalie — Wikipedia","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Caudalie"},{"title":"Caudalie — Grokipedia","url":"https://grokipedia.com/page/Caudalie"},{"title":"Caudalie - Wikipedia","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Caudalie"}]},"angle":{"goal":"Skin","chain":["Apply grape-polyphenol serums and creams","Antioxidant and hydrating skin support","Brighter, smoother-looking skin"],"effect":"claimed","text":"Caudalie products are used as everyday skincare aimed at glow and an even tone. The brand's claims rest on grape-seed polyphenol research and its own testing."},"wikipedia":{"title":"Caudalie","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Caudalie"},"grokipedia":"https://grokipedia.com/page/Caudalie","lead":["Caudalie is a French skincare company founded in 1995 by Mathilde and Bertrand Thomas after research by a Bordeaux pharmacy professor, Joseph Vercauteren, showed grape-seed polyphenols could act as strong antioxidants [1][2]. Its products draw on grape and grapevine extracts from the family's Bordeaux vineyard, Smith Haut Lafitte [2].","For appearance, the pitch is antioxidant, hydrating and brightening skincare: serums, creams, masks and a facial mist. Its first Vinotherapie spa opened in 1999 [1][2].","Lines named in coverage include the Beauty Elixir mist (1997), Vinoperfect brightening (2005), Premier Cru anti-ageing (2009) and Resveratrol-Lift (2020), with Vinopure for oily skin [1]."],"infobox":[["Type","Skincare brand"],["Founded","1995, Bordeaux, France [1][2]"],["Founders","Mathilde and Bertrand Thomas [1][2]"],["Signature ingredient","Grape-seed polyphenols [1]"],["First spa","Vinotherapie, 1999 [1][2]"]],"sections":[{"h":"History","paras":["The founders noticed grape harvest effects on skin and met Professor Vercauteren in 1993, which led to the brand's launch in 1995 [1]. The first Vinotherapie Spa opened in 1999 at Les Sources de Caudalie [1][2]."],"subs":[]},{"h":"Products","paras":["Skincare, body care, fragrance and masks based on grape and grapevine ingredients [2]. The company describes most ranges as 95% natural-origin [1]."],"subs":[]},{"h":"Clinical studies","paras":["No studies found."],"subs":[]}],"lore":null,"timeline":[{"year":"1993","event":"Founders meet Professor Joseph Vercauteren [1]."},{"year":"1995","event":"Caudalie launched [1][2]."},{"year":"1999","event":"First Vinotherapie Spa opens [1][2]."}],"refs":[{"title":"Caudalie","url":"https://grokipedia.com/page/Caudalie","source":"Grokipedia","year":2025,"type":"encyclopedia"},{"title":"Caudalie","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Caudalie","source":"Wikipedia","year":2024,"type":"encyclopedia"}],"studies":[],"reddit":[],"forums":[]}